{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleDecomposition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"CycleDecomposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18CycleDecompositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A counting sort of f gives the preimage rows and the in-degrees. Peeling the vertices of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in-degree zero, repeatedly, visits the tree vertices leaves first, summing subtree sizes on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the way, and leaves exactly the cyclic ones; each cycle is then walked from its least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex. Revisiting the peeled vertices in reverse, parents first, gives every tail length","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and root and a preorder numbering of the trees from the subtree sizes; a counting sort by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"depth then lays out the level-ancestor table. Nothing recurses or chases a chain of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dependent reads, so a tail of 10⁷ vertices needs no call stack.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph has fewer than 2³¹ vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/cycledecomposition()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The cycles of the graph, and every vertex’s tail, root and preimages. O(n) time, with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allocation per vertex. The result holds 5n + 3 ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s (two ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arrays for the preimage","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows, one for the vertices by depth, a 12-byte record per vertex and a 4-byte preorder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number beside each vertex by depth), plus one per cycle and one per unit of the longest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tail; building it takes 3n more for a moment (two 12-byte entries per vertex).","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18cycleDecompositionAC05CycleE0VyF","remoteSource":{"fileName":"CycleDecomposition.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/FunctionalGraphs\/CycleDecomposition.swift#L346"},"title":"cycleDecomposition()","extendedModule":"FunctionalGraphs","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleDecomposition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"CycleDecomposition","preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18CycleDecompositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"FunctionalGraphs"}]},"references":{"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs":{"kind":"symbol","title":"FunctionalGraphs","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs","abstract":[],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs"},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/FunctionalGraph/CycleDecomposition":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Every cycle of a functional graph, and for each vertex its tail and the cycle it reaches, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Flajolet and Odlyzko’s terms: walking from ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the first vertex on a cycle is ","type":"text"},{"code":"root(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"tailLength(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" steps away, on a cycle of ","type":"text"},{"code":"cycleLength(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices. For a permutation, ","type":"text"},{"code":"cycles","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is its cycle decomposition and every tail is zero.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CycleDecomposition","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"FunctionalGraph.CycleDecomposition","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/cycledecomposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CycleDecomposition","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/FunctionalGraph/cycleDecomposition()":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleDecomposition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV18CycleDecompositionV","text":"CycleDecomposition","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","abstract":[{"text":"The cycles of the graph, and every vertex’s tail, root and preimages. O(n) time, with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allocation per vertex. The result holds 5n + 3 ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s (two ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arrays for the preimage","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows, one for the vertices by depth, a 12-byte record per vertex and a 4-byte preorder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number beside each vertex by depth), plus one per cycle and one per unit of the longest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tail; building it takes 3n more for a moment (two 12-byte entries per vertex).","type":"text"}],"title":"cycleDecomposition()","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph\/cycledecomposition()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://FunctionalGraphs/documentation/FunctionalGraphs/FunctionalGraph":{"kind":"symbol","title":"FunctionalGraph","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph of a function f on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":": every vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" has exactly one out-edge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v → f(v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a fixed point is a self-loop. Also called a successor graph."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}]}}}